        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "ABSTRACT",
      "pageStart": 4,
      "pageEnd": 4,
      "target": "../sections/sec-000-abstract.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The economic crisis has led to increased demand and reduced resources for health sectors. The trend for increasing \nhealthcare costs to individuals, the health sector and wider society is significant. Public health can be part of the \nsolution to this challenge. The evidence shows that prevention can be cost-effective, provide value for money and \ngive returns on investment in both the short and longer terms. This public health summary outlines quick returns on \ninvestment for health and other sectors for interventions that promote physical activity and healthy employment; \naddress housing and",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
